      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐκείνοις μὲν ἀντὶ τοῦ πολλοῦ μόχθου παρέσχον τὸ μὴ πλανηθῆναι, ἐξὸν μὴ μοχθῆσαι",
          "english_quote": "they have given those people, in exchange for their great toil, only the benefit of not being led astray, though the toil could have been avoided",
          "issue": "“Only the benefit” makes not being led astray the exclusive benefit received. The Greek identifies this return for their toil but does not expressly exclude other benefits. μέν participates in the contrast between those who understood and those who were misled; it does not supply this restriction. The criticism of unnecessary toil remains clear without adding “only.”",
          "suggested_revision": "Delete “only”: “they have given those people, in exchange for their great toil, the benefit of not being led astray, though the toil could have been avoided.” Submit the revised wording for fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
