      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἅπερ ὑπὸ μόνης ὑπερβαλλούσης φρονήσεως γενέσθαι δυνατὸν ἐστιν καὶ καταληφθῆναι ὑπὸ ἐπιστήμης τῆς μόνης ταῦτα ἀκριβοῦν δυναμένης.",
          "english_quote": "These can be brought about only by surpassing intelligence and can be comprehended only by knowledge capable of determining them precisely.",
          "issue": "The second μόνης belongs to the attributive phrase describing knowledge as alone capable of determining these things precisely. The draft transfers that exclusivity to “can be comprehended,” introducing a restriction there while failing to preserve its stated attachment to the capability of knowledge. The two occurrences of μόνης should retain their distinct grammatical scopes.",
